Hardware requirements
=====================
- Type-C USB cable
- Two FRDM-IMXRT1186 boards
- Personal Computer

Board settings
============
To Enable FlexSPI Follower:
R113, R117, R131~133, R135, R160~R163, R182 Change to 1-3.
Connect the J39 of two boards with cable.
Note: ​As a high-speed bus requiring signal integrity, this external connection may not support optimal performance.​

Prepare the Demo
===============
1.  Connect a USB cable between the host PC and the UART port(J189) on the target board.
2.  Connect a J-Link debuger between the host PC and the JTAG port(J205) on the target board.
3.  Open a serial terminal with the following settings:
    - 115200 baud rate
    - 8 data bits
    - No parity
    - One stop bit
    - No flow control
4.  Download the program to the target board.
5.  Either press the reset button on your board or launch the debugger in your IDE to begin running the demo.

Running the demo
===============
When the example runs successfully, you can see the similar information from the terminal as below.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Default project uses Follower code. Define EXAMPLE_RUN_FLEXSPI_LEADER in project to run leader code.

